    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d237">

                <pb facs="0272" n="182" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1898</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-05-31T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 31, 1918, 4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4289. Your 4033, May 29, 11 p.m. There seems to be no justification for a change
                    in the policy of this Government. You will please keep us fully and frequently
                    advised of the conference and its developments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
